{
  "_comment": [
    "The managers a candidate is actually asked about. Edit this file, not sync_funds.py.",
    "",
    "'search' is the query put to EDGAR's own company search (browse-edgar, filtered to",
    "form 13F-HR). 'match' pins the answer when that search returns more than one filer,",
    "and holds EDGAR's conformed name exactly as EDGAR spells it. 'cik' is filled in by",
    "`python3 scripts/sync_funds.py --resolve`; it is never typed by hand, so every number",
    "here traces back to a search anyone can repeat.",
    "",
    "'name' is what the site shows and 'strategy' is the bucket it shows it under.",
    "",
    "Index managers are deliberately absent. BlackRock, Vanguard and State Street are the",
    "three largest 13F filers by a wide margin and tell a candidate nothing: they hold",
    "everything, in proportion to the index, because that is the mandate.",
    "",
    "'id' is the manager's identity and the last part of its URL. It is fixed: renaming",
    "'name' never moves a page. 'cik' is the filer reporting the manager now.",
    "",
    "'filers' is for a manager that has reported under more than one CIK: a new reporting",
    "entity (a listed parent, a holding company after a take-private) or a re-registration.",
    "Each filer reports the quarters ending between its 'from' and 'to' dates, and the",
    "windows may not overlap. 'evidence' says how the hand-over is known; 'check' says what",
    "an editor compared before adopting a successor whose book could differ in size."
  ],
